    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d444">

                <pb facs="0609" n="503" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg503"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Minister Morgan.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-11-23"><hi rendition="#italic">November 23,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 91.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 259, of the 9th instant, reporting that, according to a recent decision of
                    the supreme court of Cuba, the rights of the owner of a foreign patent are not
                    impaired by registration of it in Cuba by another person.</p>
                <p>Copies of your dispatch have been forwarded to the Interior Department and the
                    Merchants’ Association of New York, and it has been suggested to the latter body
                    that steps might be taken to bring a test case of piracy of a trade-mark before
                    the supreme court of Cuba.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
